## Boundaries

- `cmd/wat` is thin CLI wiring; behavior belongs in `cmd/wat/internal/*`.
- `sdk/run` owns dispatch and registration inspection.
- Native SDKs own native wire contracts and never import `sdk/agnostic`.
- `sdk/agnostic` exposes only truthful cross-agent behavior and adapts onto all
  three native SDKs.
- `internal/hookkit` is module-private machinery, not a public convenience API.
- Install/test/doctor get registration identity from `run.Inspect`.
- Every registerable hook package has `bind.go` for `RegisterHandler`
  (observe-only → `RegisterObserve`; result-emitting → `RegisterWith`).
  `event.go` holds types and codec register/decode only — never
  `RegisterHandler`. Observe-only omits `results.go`/`output.go`, not `bind.go`.
- Follow
  [Native hook layout](../../CONTRIBUTING.md#native-hook-layout) for codec
  normalization and field-presence handling.

## Public changes

Ship tests, godoc, guides, and changelog updates with public behavior. Every
exported identifier needs lead-name godoc; follow
[CONTRIBUTING.md](../../CONTRIBUTING.md#documentation-and-godoc) for the
canonical rule. Keep registrations and package initialization free of external
side effects.

## Version pinning

Use exact tool and Action versions (`@vN.N.N` only for Actions). When one
dependency changes, update every reference to that dependency in the same
change. Audit floating major or minor tags with:

```bash
rg 'uses:\s*[\w./-]+@v\d+(\.\d+)?$' .github/workflows
```

No matches are allowed.
